WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:18.004
Bobby met Ms. Folani in the hallway on his way to Kids Central.

2
00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:20.780
"Hello, Bobby," she said.

3
00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:23.870
"I saw your mom the other day at the grocery store.

4
00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:26.236
She is so cheerful and nice.

5
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:31.282
Do you have anything special planned for Mother's Day?"

6
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:37.016
Bobby swallowed. "Oh. Mother's Day . . . When is that?"

7
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:41.132
Ms. Folani laughed. "It's next Sunday, Bobby!

8
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.823
You have 12 days.

9
00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:53.723
I'm sure you'll think of something sweet!"

10
00:00:53.724 --> 00:00:57.279
"Maybe we'll make something for Mother's Day in Kids Central,"

11
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.519
Bobby thought as he opened the gym door.

12
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:09.386
While Miss Shelly was setting up the tables, Bobby asked Jason what he was doing for his mom on Mother's Day.

13
00:01:09.387 --> 00:01:13.627
"My dad and I are going to bake her a cake," Jason said.

14
00:01:13.628 --> 00:01:15.990
"Why? What are you doing?"

15
00:01:15.991 --> 00:01:18.518
Miss Shelly blew her whistle.

16
00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:23.112
"Please put away your things and come over," she called.

17
00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:26.877
Miss Shelly passed out paper cups.

18
00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:33.841
"Today we are going to turn these paper cups into flowerpots," said Miss Shelly.

19
00:01:33.842 --> 00:01:38.416
"How do we turn them into flowerpots?" Izzie wanted to know.

20
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:43.096
"By planting flower seeds in them!" said Miss Shelly.

21
00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:49.147
"What kind of flower seeds are we planting?" Bobby asked.

22
00:01:49.148 --> 00:01:51.739
Moms always like flowers.

23
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.551
Maybe this could be his present.

24
00:01:54.552 --> 00:01:59.645
Miss Shelly held up a bag. "Marigolds," she said.

25
00:01:59.646 --> 00:02:01.865
Then she showed them a picture.

26
00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:08.168
"Marigolds are small plants with green leaves and yellow-orange flowers."

27
00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:12.461
"Those would be perfect for my mom, don't you think?"

28
00:02:12.462 --> 00:02:14.646
Bobby whispered to Jason.

29
00:02:14.647 --> 00:02:16.202
"I guess so.

30
00:02:16.203 --> 00:02:21.053
How about getting her a video game?" Jason said.

31
00:02:21.054 --> 00:02:26.869
"Jason, moms like chocolate, not video games," Izzie said.

32
00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.726
Miss Shelly tapped the table with her pencil.

33
00:02:29.727 --> 00:02:34.510
"First use your pencil to poke a hole in the bottom of your paper cup.

34
00:02:34.511 --> 00:02:39.535
That way when we water the plants, the extra water can drain out.

35
00:02:39.536 --> 00:02:42.541
Next fill the cup with soil.

36
00:02:42.542 --> 00:02:46.834
Please go and dip your cup into that box of soil over there."

37
00:02:46.835 --> 00:02:54.109
Miss Shelly pointed to a box on the floor.

38
00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.569
"Then we dig a little hole with our fingers and put the seeds in, right?" Izzie said.

39
00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.152
She had planted flowers with her mom before.

40
00:03:03.153 --> 00:03:06.900
"Exactly!" Miss Shelly said.

41
00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:15.361
She gave each kid a few seeds.

42
00:03:15.362 --> 00:03:19.905
"After that we give them water and sun.

43
00:03:19.906 --> 00:03:23.287
And we wait for them to grow!"

44
00:03:23.288 --> 00:03:27.385
"Wait for them to grow?" Bobby thought nervously.

45
00:03:27.386 --> 00:03:32.072
He had forgotten that it took a long time for seeds to turn into plants.

46
00:03:32.073 --> 00:03:34.611
"Miss Shelly?" Bobby asked.

47
00:03:34.612 --> 00:03:38.118
"Will our marigolds bloom by Mother's Day?"

48
00:03:38.119 --> 00:03:40.393
"I'm afraid not, Bobby.

49
00:03:40.394 --> 00:03:44.739
It takes a month or two for them to grow," Miss Shelly answered.

50
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:49.166
"Oh no . . ." Bobby's heart sank.

51
00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.814
Now he had nothing to give his mom for Mother's Day.

52
00:03:52.815 --> 00:03:57.298
"I know! You could give the pot to her next Sunday anyway.

53
00:03:57.299 --> 00:04:04.141
And then when the flowers bloom, it will be like Mother's Day all over again!" Nina said.

54
00:04:04.142 --> 00:04:07.255
Bobby smiled. What a great idea!

55
00:04:07.256 --> 00:04:15.003
That's just what he'd do.
